meta {
  name: Print Label
  type: http
  seq: 38
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/accession/order-samples/print-label
  body: json
  auth: bearer
}

headers {
  content-type: application/json
}

auth:bearer {
  token: {{businessAccessToken}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "sampleId": "{{sampleId}}",
    "templateId": "{{pdfReportTemplateId}}"
  }
}

docs {
  Render one accession sample's barcode label to a PDF (`order_label_print`),
  streamed back as `application/pdf`. The backend builds the label context from the
  sample's real data — `barcode` (rendered as TEXT, not a scannable image),
  `accession_no`, `order_code`, patient, `sample_type`, and the joined `tests`.

  ## Body
  - `sampleId` (required) — the accession sample to label.
  - `templateId` (optional) — the `order_label_print` template to render with. Omit
    to let the backend resolve it: the Configuration default for the
    `order_label_print` slot (active branch, then tenant-wide), else the first
    active `order_label_print` template. Having more than one active template is
    fine — the configured (else first) one is used.

  ## Errors
  - 404 `ACCESSION_SAMPLE_NOT_FOUND` — sample missing / soft-deleted / other tenant.
  - 404 `NO_ACTIVE_PRINT_TEMPLATE` — no `templateId` supplied and no active
    `order_label_print` template exists to fall back to.

  In Bruno, use "Save Response → Save to file" to inspect the PDF.
}
